course: dictionary
lesson: 622
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is used by reading the words around it, which is the context. «A babe in arms» is a very small baby, because arms are where you hold a little baby.
explain: Babe can also be a loving name. Adults may say «Thanks, babe» to a partner, and a parent may call a child «babe» in the same warm way as «darling» or «honey». The sentence tells you who is speaking and how they feel.
explain: Some slang uses of babe are rude. In those, it is used to mean an attractive person, and many people find that disrespectful. Good readers notice when a word feels wrong in a sentence, then check a dictionary.
fact: Babe means a baby, especially in older books, carols and Bible stories.
fact: «The babe in the manger» means the baby Jesus.
fact: «A babe in the woods» means someone innocent who does not know how the world works.
fact: Used as a loving name, «babe» is like «darling» or «honey».
fact: Some slang uses of babe are disrespectful, so do not use it to talk about how someone looks.
exercise: In the carol, «the babe in the manger» is a baby. Who is the baby? | A puppy in a barn | A farm pig | A sleepy shepherd | *The baby Jesus
exercise: Coco says, «Yeah, it's vintage, babe.» What is babe used as here? | A place to shop | A word for a farm animal | *A friendly word between friends | A baby in arms
exercise: Find the meaning of «a babe in arms». | *A very young baby | A sleepy horse | A grown-up who is always cross | Someone lost in the woods
test: «A babe in the woods» means someone who... | Is always asleep | Is scared of the dark | *Is innocent and does not know how the world works | Is very good at finding their way
test: Jess is going round the shops with older girls. Why might she need to be careful with the word babe? | Babe only means a pig | *Some slang uses are rude and can be disrespectful | Babe means a shop | Older girls never shop
exam: Which use of babe is a loving name? | A babe in the woods means someone innocent | A babe in arms is a baby | *Love you, babe, said to a partner | The babe in the manger
